   "id": 631722,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<p>Old Faithful is a geyser in Yellowstone National Park. The following table offers some rough estimates of the length of an eruption (in minutes) and the amount of water (in gallons) in that eruption.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n  <thead></thead>\n  <tbody>\n              <tr>\n                <th scope=\"row\">\n                  Length (minutes)\n                </th>\n                <td>\n                  1.5\n                </td>\n                <td>\n                  2\n                </td>\n                <td>\n                  3\n                </td>\n                <td>\n                  4.5\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <th scope=\"row\">\n                  Amount of Water\n                      (gallons)\n                </th>\n                <td>\n                  3,700\n                </td>\n                <td>\n                  4,100\n                </td>\n                <td>\n                  6,450\n                </td>\n                <td>\n                  8,400\n                </td>\n              </tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n<br> <p>Use technology to find an equation of the line of best fit. Round to the nearest hundredth.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
